# What `gcloud run deploy --source backend` uploads to the Cloud Build bucket.
#
# Without this file gcloud uploads this whole directory: .env (live
# service-role key and other secrets) and .venv (hundreds of MB) ended up in the
# build source archive. The image itself only ever copied app/ (see
# Dockerfile), so nothing here changes what runs, only what is uploaded.
.gcloudignore
.git
.gitignore
.env
*.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
tests/
